👷🏼‍♀️Under the hood
Here is how you can write your own function. You don’t need to but it is good to know what is happening behind the scenes.

# x hoch y
power &lt;- function(x, y) {
  result &lt;- x^y
  return(result)
}

x &lt;- 1:4
# Call the function
power(x, 2)
#&gt; [1]  1  4  9 16
power(x, 3)
#&gt; [1]  1  8 27 64

But, functions can do anything you want and there are functions for almost anything:

# bc why not
voice &lt;- function(x){
  if (x == "cat") {
    say &lt;- "miau"
  } else if (x == "dog"){
    say &lt;- "wof wof"
  } else {
    say &lt;- "???"
  }
  return(say)
}

nelly &lt;- "cat"
voice(nelly)
#&gt; [1] "miau"
voice("dog")
#&gt; [1] "wof wof"
voice("capybara")
#&gt; [1] "???"
